<title>UK: B.A.T stumbles on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>B.A.T stumbles on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries slipped on profit-taking as the broad stock market rose, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1144 GMT, the shares were off 8-1/2p to 482p on volume of almost 2.6 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;Volume has dried up noticeably today. It seems all the U.S. buyers are finished for the time being,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>He said the lack of U.S. buyers and the recent round of profit-taking in U.S. tobacco shares kept a lid on B.A.T shares.</p>
<p>-- Debra Sherman, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
